---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import Showcase from "../components/Showcase.astro";
---
<Base title="Aerie: a self-hosted knowledge base for IT teams"
      description="Aerie gathers your IT team's fixes, runbooks and know-how into one knowledge base, filed by team, versioned and searchable, on a server you own.">

<div class="hero">
  <div class="head">
    <h1>Everything your IT team knows, finally in one place.</h1>
    <p>Fixes hide in old email threads, chat history, sticky notes and the heads of your most experienced people. Aerie gets it all into one knowledge base, filed by team, versioned and searchable, on a server you own, so it's still there when someone is out sick, on vacation or moving on.</p>
  </div>
  <Showcase />
</div>

<section class="sec" id="spaces" aria-labelledby="spaces-h">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="split">
      <div>
        <h2 id="spaces-h">A secure space for every team</h2>
        <p class="lede">Each team keeps its knowledge in a space of its own: private by default, shared when you decide. Open a space to another team, to everyone who signs in, or to the public.</p>
        <p class="note">The team's lead owns the space. Access is granted by group, so membership stays with the people who manage identity. Supervisors keep its content in order, Contributors write, and Readers read. Need something in between? Add a custom role.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="panel">
        <div class="ph">Roles in a space <span>per person or group</span></div>
        <table class="roles">
          <tr><th scope="row">Reader</th><td>Reads the pages in the space.</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">Contributor</th><td>Writes pages, and moves or deletes their own work.</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">Supervisor</th><td>Moves and deletes anyone's pages in the space.</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">Owner</th><td>Accountable for the space and its settings.</td></tr>
        </table>
      </div>
    </div>

    <dl class="rows">
      <div><dt>Curated knowledge</dt><dd>Every page can name its owner and the systems it applies to, so readers know who stands behind it.</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Automatic ageing</dt><dd>Set a review cycle per space. Each page shows the date it is next due, so old runbooks don't go unnoticed.</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Document revision history</dt><dd>Identify changes between versions of a document, and restore previous versions.</dd></div>
      <div><dt>A capable editor</dt><dd>Code blocks, tables, images and attachments, with drafts until a page is ready.</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Search that forgives typos</dt><dd>Find the spooler fix even when you type "spoolr".</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Tags and export</dt><dd>Tag pages by server, app or topic. Export to PDF, Word, CSV or Excel.</dd></div>
    </dl>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="sec" id="ai" aria-labelledby="ai-h">
  <div class="wrap split">
    <div>
      <h2 id="ai-h">AI that works under your rules</h2>
      <p class="lede">Connect Aerie to the model you choose, including one on your own network.</p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <ul class="mech">
        <li><b>AI import</b><span>Drop in any documentation you already have and get formatted, easy-to-read documentation back, automatically, with full control of the review and save process.</span></li>
        <li><b>AI format</b><span>One click puts a rough page into a clean, consistent layout without changing what it says.</span></li>
        <li><b>AI assist</b><span>Paste notes, screenshots or files into the editor. Aerie builds the page from them, or merges them into the page you're working on.</span></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="sec" id="security" aria-labelledby="security-h">
  <div class="wrap split">
    <div>
      <h2 id="security-h">Locked down by default</h2>
      <p class="lede">Runbooks hold server names, recovery steps and who to call. Aerie is designed to keep them in the right hands, and it's tested against attack as it's built.</p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <ul class="mech">
        <li><b>Sensitive spaces</b><span>Mark a space sensitive and it's closed to Admins too. An Admin who needs in uses emergency access, which is logged, and the space's Owners are told.</span></li>
        <li><b>A tamper-evident audit log</b><span>Each entry is hash-chained to the one before it, so an edited or deleted entry breaks the chain. Ship the log to your SIEM.</span></li>
        <li><b>Scoped API tokens</b><span>Tokens carry only the permissions you give them, and they expire.</span></li>
        <li><b>OAuth 2.0 for applications</b><span>Connect other applications without sharing passwords. An Admin registers each one, each user approves it, and access can be cut off at any time.</span></li>
        <li><b>Built and tested to OWASP standards</b><span>Aerie is developed against the OWASP Top 10 and tested with OWASP methods. Automated tests try actions under every role and confirm the wrong ones are refused, and the running app is scanned for vulnerabilities, with findings fixed before release.</span></li>
        <li><b>Sign-in</b><span>One-time codes from an authenticator app at sign-in. Signing out ends every session for that account.</span></li>
      </ul>
      <div class="panel audit">
        <div class="ph">Audit log <span>sample entries</span></div>
        <div class="wide">
          <table class="mono">
            <tr><td>2026-11-12 22:41</td><td>admin.pat</td><td>Emergency access: Security Operations</td><td>9f3c…e1a0</td></tr>
            <tr><td>2026-11-12 22:41</td><td>system</td><td>Owners notified: Security Operations</td><td>2b77…09cd</td></tr>
            <tr><td>2026-11-12 22:58</td><td>admin.pat</td><td>Viewed: Ransomware Playbook</td><td>c41e…7f52</td></tr>
          </table>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="sec" id="install" aria-labelledby="install-h">
  <div class="wrap split">
    <div>
      <h2 id="install-h">Runs on your server</h2>
      <p class="lede">No cloud service sits behind Aerie. Your pages stay on hardware you control, and it's free to self-host.</p>
      <p class="note">Already running a commercial knowledge base? Aerie is built for maximum compatibility with existing commercial solutions, so it can drop in as a replacement with minimal effort. Your scripts and integrations keep working.</p>
      <p class="note">An install guide comes with the first release. Until then, the live demo runs the current build.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="hosts">
      <div>
        <h3>Windows Server</h3>
        <ul><li>Runs under IIS</li><li>SQL Server database</li></ul>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3>Docker</h3>
        <ul><li>One container image</li><li>A single SQLite file, or SQL Server</li></ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="sec" id="features" aria-labelledby="features-h">
  <div class="wrap">
    <h2 id="features-h">Feature set</h2>
    <p class="lede">Everything below is in the current build, and you can try all of it in the live demo.</p>
    <div class="panel feat">
      <table class="roles">
        <tr><th scope="row">Knowledge</th><td>Team spaces with folder trees. Editor with code blocks, tables, images and attachments. Drafts, full version history with compare and restore, and a recycle bin.</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row">Curation</th><td>Page owners, review cycles with due dates, and tags. An application inventory links each app and version to its servers and its pages.</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row">Finding and sharing</th><td>Search that forgives typos. Export pages to PDF or Word, and tables to CSV or Excel.</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row">Access</th><td>Four roles per space plus your own custom roles, for people or groups. Spaces can be private, open to signed-in users, or public.</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row">Security</th><td>Sensitive spaces with logged emergency access. Sign-in codes. A hash-chained audit log that ships to your SIEM. Scoped, expiring API tokens.</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row">AI</th><td>Import, format and assist, on the model you choose. An Admin controls each feature, and a person approves every result.</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row">Compatibility</th><td>Maximum compatibility with existing commercial solutions, for a drop-in replacement with minimal effort. REST API, with OAuth 2.0 for connected applications.</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row">Extending</th><td>Plugins bring their own screens and data. Theme colors for Day and Night, set by an Admin.</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row">Deployment</th><td>Windows Server with IIS and SQL Server, or one Docker image with SQLite or SQL Server. Free to self-host.</td></tr>
      </table>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="close" aria-labelledby="close-h">
  <h2 id="close-h">See it for yourself</h2>
  <p>Check out the live demo. Sign in, look around and try it on real pages.</p>
  <a class="btn" href="https://demo.aeriekb.com">Live Demo</a>
</section>

</Base>
